oping to scare him  back to Hong Kong the gangsters take Lee  out behind the restaurant where he grabs  a wooden pole and shows off some bo  staff skills when more punks show up to  the party armed with chains and  switchblades Lee pulls out two pairs of  nunchucks and we all know exactly how  that goes  [Music]  then and perhaps the funniest scene in  any Bruce Lee movie a gangster gets his  own pair of nunchucks and tries to beat  Bruce Lee at his own game but he only  succeeds in whacking himself in the head  then when Lee goes back to the  restaurant to rescue his friends he  takes out some thugs with homemade  wooden darts Lee might not understand  Italian customs but he certainly knows  how to mess up some mobsters what do you  do when all your henchmen can't beat  Bruce Lee well if you're the evil crime  boss from way of the Dragon  you hired Chuck Norris of course he will  be the one who will personally take care  of that time the two legends Throwdown  in the Coliseum and after some pre  fights stretching the Battle of the  Titans begins Norris is absolutely  ferocious and it's clear this guy has  the strength advantage he drops leave  with a spinning roundhouse kick lands a  solid combination of elbows and body  shots and then judo tosses Lee to the  floor but everything changes when Lee  starts dancing around the Coliseum like  he's Muhammad Ali the movement makes all  the difference and the flat-footed  Norris can't keep up in a beautiful  slow-motion sequence we watch Lee dodge  and parry blows before unleashing a  stunning four kick combo that turns the  fight in his favor  eventually Lee brings the greatest  martial arts showdown to a close by  killing Norris with a sick guillotine  choke the movie that turned Bruce Lee  into an international star Enter the  Dragon follows our high-kicking hero as  he's tasked with joining a mysterious  martial arts tournament and bringing  down the criminal kingpin running the  contest but the stakes are personal for  Lee one of the competitors is  responsible for the death of Lee's  sister so when the two are pitted  against each other  Lee isn't going to turn the other cheek  played by martial artist Bob wall O'Hara  is the psycho on Lee's hit list the dude  has an attitude as big as the scar  running down his face and when he  squares off against Lee he tries to make  a big impression by punching a wooden  board in half but Lee isn't fazed and  famously tells his opponent oh don't  back Bruce Lee on the other hand hits  back a whole lot every time they face  off Lee lands the first blow and then he  sends O'Hara soaring with a scary  slow-mo kick infuriated O'Hara grabs  some broken bottles and plans on carving  Lee up but after a well-placed kicked  the jaw Lee jumps on the dudes head and  breaks O'Hara's neck after a whole bunch  of kung-fu battles throughout Enter the  Dragon the villainous han and leif  finally square off in the film's big  showdown a scene filled with classic  Bruce Lee moments there's the kick from  hell that nearly decapitates Han there's  the scorpion kick that leaves the  villain hurting and humiliated and then  there's the insane scene in which a  freshly cut Lee licks his own bloody  fingers to prove he's a savage finally  the showdown moves into a Hall of  Mirrors where Han uses the reflections  to his advantage hiding in plain sight  but after remembering some words of  wisdom from his old teacher Lee smashes  all the glass so there's nowhere left  for Honda hide the crazy scene comes to  an end when Lee side kicks Han so hard  that he flies straight into a spear Game  of Death is one of the biggest what-ifs  in movie history Lee only shot 40  minutes of the film before his untimely  death but his vision sounds epic the  plot was going to follow Lee as he  fought his way up a pagoda in search of  a valuable treasure each time he reached  a new floor who would face a new boss  who specialized in a specific martial  art Lee would have to overcome 